e next digit (billions place).\n\nPutting all the digits together from right to left (units to hundred millions and then billions):\n\nStarting from the units digit:\n\nUnits (position9):7\n\nTens (position8):8\n\nHundreds (position7):0\n\nThousands (position6):0\n\nTen thousands (position5):0\n\nHundred thousands (position4):8\n\nMillions (position3):8\n\nTen millions (position2):8\n\nHundred millions (position1):6\n\nPlus the carryover1 in the billions place.\n\nSo arranging from highest to lowest place:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:6\n\nTen millions:8\n\nMillions:8\n\nHundred thousands:8\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nThousands:0\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:8\n\nUnits:7\n\nWait, hold on, let me list them in order:\n\nThe digits from billions down to units:\n\nBillions digit:1\n\nHundred millions:6\n\nTen millions:8\n\nMillions:8\n\nHundred thousands:8 (from position4 which was 8)\n\nWait, position4 was hundred thousands place, which we had written as 8. But in the sequence above, after hundred thousands comes ten thousands, which was 0. Wait, perhaps I need to list each digit step by step:\n\nLet me list each digit position's result:\n\nStarting from the billions place (the final carryover):1\n\nThen the hundred millions place:6\n\nThen ten millions:8\n\nMillions:8\n\nHundred thousands:8 (from position4)\n\nTen thousands:0 (from position5)\n\nThousands:0 (from position6)\n\nHundreds:0 (from position7)\n\nTens:8 (position8)\n\nUnits:7 (position9)\n\nWait, but the hundred thousands place (position4) was 8, ten thousands (position5) was 0, thousands (position6) was 0, etc.\n\nTherefore, the number is:\n\n1 (billions), 6 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 7 (units).\n\nSo written out as:\n\n1,688,080,087?\n\nWait let's see:\n\nBreaking down:\n\nBillions:1,\n\nHundred millions:6,\n\nTen millions:8,\n\nMillions:8,\n\nHundred thousands:8,\n\nTen thousands:0,\n\nThousands:0,\n\nHundre